<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal BCP says no talks on M.Confianca.</title>
<headline>Portugal BCP says no talks on M.Confianca.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Comercial Portugues (BCP) is not in negotiations with anybody about its 20 percent stake in Mundial Confianca, the insurer that acts as holding for the financial interests of the Champalimaud group, BCP chairman Jorge Jardim Goncalves said in an interview.</p>
<p>&quot;At the moment, we are not negotiating anything,&quot; he told Diario Economico.</p>
<p>&quot;As I always said, it is a stable stake. One day we will take a look at it. It is an important asset,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Jardim Goncalves said that the group was looking for a partner in China and another in Brazil.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3113121</p>
</text>
